From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: free wifili exception skbs with dev_kfree_skb_any()

The wifili SoC extended-data callback discards every exception it does not
handle with kfree(), not with an skb free. kfree() returns the sk_buff struct
to the allocator on its own, so skb_release_data() never runs: the linear data
buffer is leaked outright, along with any page fragments and the destructor.
One buffer per exception frame, unbounded over uptime.

MIC errors are the only type handled, so the default arm takes every
NSS_WIFILI_SOC_EXT_DATA_PKT_MSDU_LINK_DESC, _INVALID_PEER, _2K_JUMP_ERROR and
_WIFI_PARSE_ERROR the firmware raises - 2K jumps and parse errors are routine
on a loaded radio, and _INVALID_PEER fires whenever the firmware sees a frame
for a peer the host has just torn down.

The mesh offload patch already carries this fix, but package/kernel/mac80211
applies nss/mesh only under CONFIG_ATH11K_NSS_MESH_SUPPORT, so the correct free
reaches mesh builds alone and every other NSS build keeps the leak. Fix it in
the wifili path itself, where the callback lives.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
index f101919..4235a84 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -535,7 +535,7 @@
 		ath11k_nss_process_mic_error(ab, skb);
 		break;
 	default:
-		kfree(skb);
+		dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
 		break;
 	}
 }
